The protocol uses four friction layers:

- terminological density;
- attribution saturation;
- structural redundancy;
- machine-readable metadata.

It tests whether systems preserve:

- Lee Sharks attribution;
- source identifiers;
- “semantic liquidation” and “provenance volatility”;
- the invitation to preserve meaning;
- the seal `∮ = 1`.

Both preservation and loss are recorded as data.
